#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198096 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198279 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c23caadd-1738-549f-aade-2c983dc250dc" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Truth Set of a Predicate"}] :question/id #uuid "4b253527-f5ca-5927-97f0-d91491d598b3" :question/math-academy-id "e-12721" :question/problem "Find the truth set of the following predicate:\n\n$\\qquad$ $P(x):$ $x^2+2x=3$\n\nwhere the universal set is $\\mathbb{Z}.$" :question/worked-solution "The *truth set* of a predicate $P(x)$ is the set of elements in its universal set $U$ such that substituting these elements for the variable makes the predicate a true statement:\n\n$$\nT = \\big\\{ x \\in U \\: | \\: P(x) \\big\\}\n$$\n\nThe universal set for our predicate is $U = \\mathbb{Z}.$\n\nWe need to find $x \\in U$ such that the following is true:\n\n$\\qquad$ $x^2+2x=3$\n\nNow, we solve the above equation by factoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+2x & =3 \\\\ {x}^{2}+2x-3 & =0 \\\\ (x+3)(x-1) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solutions are $x=-3\\in\\mathbb Z$ and $x=1\\in\\mathbb Z.$\n\nTherefore, the truth set of our predicate is $T = \\{-3,1\\}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198097 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198280 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "aa2f2ccb-45b0-5d6a-aa94-ac3eb95c745b" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Predicates of More Than One Variable"}] :question/id #uuid "14dc17f1-056e-5e82-81e6-c3964b7df2d2" :question/math-academy-id "e-12722" :question/problem "Which of the following are mathematical predicates?\n\nI. $x \\geq y$\n\nII. $\\dfrac{p}{q}$ is a rational number.\n\nIII. $a$ is a positive number." :question/worked-solution "A *predicate* of the variables $x_1,x_2,\\ldots,x_n$ is a sentence that contains the variables defined on some *universal set,* and has the property that when we substitute concrete values for all the variables into the predicate, the result becomes a statement that is either true or false.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our options. \n\n- Option I is a predicate of two variables. Substituting a concrete pair of values $(x,y)$ into the sentence, we get a statement that is either true or false.\n\n- Option II is a predicate of two variables. Substituting a concrete pair of values $(p,q)$ into the sentence, we get a statement that is either true or false.\n\n- Option III is a predicate of one variable. Substituting a concrete value for $a$ into the sentence, we get a statement that is either true or false.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198098 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198281 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9f9703bd-92ae-51f7-902b-251a7947ba6a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Truth Set of a Multivariable Predicate"}] :question/id #uuid "3d212cb2-394b-5f9d-8e7d-8406ec7ca580" :question/math-academy-id "e-12723" :question/problem "Find the truth set of the following predicate:\n\n$\\qquad$ $p \\, | \\, q$, \n\nwhere the universal set is $\\big\\{ (p,q) \\: | \\: p = 1,2,6, \\: q = 3,6,9 \\big\\}.$" :question/worked-solution "The *truth set* of a predicate $P(x_1,x_2,\\ldots,x_n)$ is the set of $n$-tuples in its universal set $U = U_1 \\times U_2 \\times \\cdots \\times U_n$ such that substituting these tuples for the variables makes the predicate a true statement:\n\n$$\nT = \\big\\{ (x_1,x_2,\\ldots,x_n) \\in U \\: | \\: P(x_1,x_2,\\ldots,x_n) \\big\\}\n$$\n\nThe universal set for our predicate is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U & =\\{1,2,6\\}\\times \\{3,6,9\\} \\\\  & =\\{(1,3),(1,6),(1,9),(2,3),(2,6),(2,9),(6,3),(6,6),(6,9)\\}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe need to find $(p,q) \\in U$ such that the following is true:\n\n$\\qquad$ $p \\, | \\, q$\n\nThe following pairs give the elements of our truth set:\n\n- $(1,3)$ since $1$ divides $3,$\n\n- $(1,6)$ since $1$ divides $6,$\n\n- $(1,9)$ since $1$ divides $9,$\n\n- $(2,6)$ since $2$ divides $6,$\n\n- $(6,6)$ since $6$ divides $6.$\n\nTherefore, the truth set of our predicate is\n\n$$\nT = \\big\\{ (1,3), (1,6), (1,9), (2,6), (6,6) \\big\\}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198721 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198280 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "aa2f2ccb-45b0-5d6a-aa94-ac3eb95c745b" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Predicates of More Than One Variable"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "704e020e-d34a-528d-9e9d-8b82289223c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459647} {:answer/id #uuid "f766b986-cfca-589d-b307-c3cfed4a40df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459648}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f766b986-cfca-589d-b307-c3cfed4a40df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459648} :answer-field/id #uuid "c8358696-c4dc-5792-a56d-b4cf06cd1f4e" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460690} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f32f7ace-9473-5adf-87d1-3a0754c1f4bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459649} {:answer/id #uuid "5764e144-7231-5741-8902-987088781ec6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459650}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5764e144-7231-5741-8902-987088781ec6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459650} :answer-field/id #uuid "9c262398-01aa-5334-93fb-2d94d63b0e3f" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460691} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a0937afd-eb79-5420-8b9b-1cc18cc13046" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459651} {:answer/id #uuid "971d785f-c08d-59dc-8767-b018db2c3a8b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459652}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a0937afd-eb79-5420-8b9b-1cc18cc13046" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459651} :answer-field/id #uuid "45cf6747-f781-581e-9df2-b7717fa5597b" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460692}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d3a9664a-054f-5dcf-9b0e-e1b4ab3dd171" :question/math-academy-id "q-174456" :question/problem "Which of the following are mathematical predicates?\n\nI. $x<y$\n\nII. $n$ is a perfect square.\n\nIII. Are $n$ and $m$ coprime?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "A *predicate* of the variables ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}$ is a sentence that contains the variables defined on some *universal set*, and has the property that when we substitute concrete values for all the variables into the predicate, the result becomes a statement that is either true or false.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our options. \n\n- Option I is a predicate of two variables. Substituting a concrete pair of values $(x,y)$ into the sentence, we get a statement that is either true or false.\n\n- Option II is a predicate of one variable. Substituting a concrete value for $n$ into the sentence, we get a statement that is either true or false.\n\n- Option III is *not* a predicate. Substituting a concrete pair of values $(n,m)$ into the sentence, we do not get a statement that is either true or false.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186425978 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198279 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c23caadd-1738-549f-aade-2c983dc250dc" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Truth Set of a Predicate"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "58b7a612-07c6-5679-8d42-d625deb5e970" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-\\infty ,4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425958} {:answer/id #uuid "d143d075-6812-5d2c-bd24-7bc7894f07b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(4,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425965} {:answer/id #uuid "d4423da0-b4c9-5f1f-83a8-6ee54f9efc80" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-4,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425966} {:answer/id #uuid "e210c4b1-8a09-558c-89b2-8405b5a063c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425970} {:answer/id #uuid "f4e815df-53f8-5522-8977-b3d95d5b221e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-\\infty ,-4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425971}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d143d075-6812-5d2c-bd24-7bc7894f07b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(4,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425965} :answer-field/id #uuid "97aeada7-12fc-5a6f-b3b8-8465455bada0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425974}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "10a98313-2524-5ce8-a6f0-176526143e93" :question/math-academy-id "q-175361" :question/problem "Find the truth set of the following predicate:\n\n$\\,$ $P(x):$ $5x+2>22,$\n\nwhere the universal set is $R.$" :question/worked-solution "The *truth set* of a predicate $P(x)$ is the set of elements in its universal set $U$ such that substituting these elements for the variable makes the predicate a true statement:\n\n$$\nT=\\{x\\in U\\,|\\,P(x)\\}\n$$\n\nWe need to find $x\\in U$ such that the following is true:\n\n$\\,$ $5x+2>22$\n\nThe universal set for our predicate is $U=R.$\n\nNow, we need to solve the above inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5x+2>22 \\\\ 5x>20 \\\\ x>4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the truth set of our predicate is\n\n$$\nT=(4,\\infty ).\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186425980 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198280 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "aa2f2ccb-45b0-5d6a-aa94-ac3eb95c745b" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Predicates of More Than One Variable"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f548d9d7-5c43-5510-85e7-89f665103530" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474544} {:answer/id #uuid "299c3818-e21a-5d63-9d43-edb435384b5a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474545}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "299c3818-e21a-5d63-9d43-edb435384b5a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474545} :answer-field/id #uuid "33029c5d-a58f-5846-b20f-d30fb9ae1431" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475198} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cffbbad6-2ff2-508a-a394-ef1effcca096" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474546} {:answer/id #uuid "966aa064-e076-50ec-9fdb-88187a6d9994" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474547}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cffbbad6-2ff2-508a-a394-ef1effcca096" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474546} :answer-field/id #uuid "8eb33668-d751-5e1f-a8f1-d04525bc5ad1" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475199} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a3099e3c-5a65-5e1b-a4c9-9aceb7935c7b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474548} {:answer/id #uuid "517d0ea8-bd34-5d06-9d04-f78f5ae6a208" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474549}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "517d0ea8-bd34-5d06-9d04-f78f5ae6a208" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474549} :answer-field/id #uuid "3bc37e72-ebc3-54f5-abd0-30ce43dacb22" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475200}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "86866e7c-73c9-5409-8743-b71ad4d3cbe4" :question/math-academy-id "q-175366" :question/problem "Which of the following are mathematical predicates?\n\nI. $P(y):$ ${y}^{2}-1=8$\n\nII. $Q(a,b):$ ${a}^{2}+{b}^{2}$\n\nIII. $R(x,y):$ $\\frac{x}{y}\\in N\\cap Q$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "A *predicate* of the variables ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}$ is a sentence that contains the variables defined on some *universal set*, and has the property that when we substitute concrete values for all the variables into the predicate, the result becomes a statement that is either true or false.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our options. \n\n- Option I is a predicate of one variable. Substituting a concrete value for $y$ into the sentence, we get a statement that is either true or false.\n\n- Option II is *not* a predicate. Substituting a concrete pair of values $(a,b)$ into the sentence, we do not get a statement that is either true or false.\n\n- Option III is a predicate of two variables. Substituting a concrete pair of values $(x,y)$ into the sentence, we get a statement that is either true or false.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186425977 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198279 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c23caadd-1738-549f-aade-2c983dc250dc" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Truth Set of a Predicate"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3cde1ebc-e432-58be-aec4-61a0a888f799" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425956} {:answer/id #uuid "4ff057a1-4c2b-565a-83cd-56aa95d66144" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-\\infty ,-3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425957} {:answer/id #uuid "5d21df02-6b8d-5e86-a2f9-f452aee05936" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-3,3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425959} {:answer/id #uuid "61c53b8b-e43b-5a05-9fb3-abadd0684739" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-3,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425960} {:answer/id #uuid "f99f6fd4-23c4-5261-9b7b-39d01859eba3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-\\infty ,3]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425972}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5d21df02-6b8d-5e86-a2f9-f452aee05936" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-3,3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425959} :answer-field/id #uuid "c5aa0841-040f-5aec-85ca-fd3f64c07a51" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425975}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0237c8ad-eb27-521a-9b96-cd671ad62b96" :question/math-academy-id "q-175372" :question/problem "Find the truth set of the following predicate:\n\n$\\,$ $P(x):$ ${x}^{2}<9$\n\nwhere the universal set is $R.$" :question/worked-solution "The *truth set* of a predicate $P(x)$ is the set of elements in its universal set $U$ such that substituting these elements for the variable makes the predicate a true statement:\n\n$$\nT=\\{x\\in U\\,|\\,P(x)\\}\n$$\n\nThe universal set for our predicate is $U=R.$\n\nWe need to find $x\\in U$ such that the following is true:\n\n$\\,$ ${x}^{2}<9$\n\nTaking the square root of both sides of the inequality, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2} & <9 \\\\ \\sqrt{{x}^{2}} & <\\sqrt{9} \\\\ |x| & <3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the definition of absolute value, we must have\n\n$$\n-3\\text{ }<x<3.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the truth set of our predicate is $T=(-3,3).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186425979 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198281 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9f9703bd-92ae-51f7-902b-251a7947ba6a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Truth Set of a Multivariable Predicate"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "13edba04-7016-55b3-998a-0c1a02b2d307" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/50/500233e26320d4faa984864948646c0a36b6a0672a3b5b5871b234f49656ac56.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425953} {:answer/id #uuid "1a94059a-c75b-54d5-86b6-d7a3d7e98d53" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/8c/8c80576fe81dd0978e5e8a4ecd937c5e71e60297dcc94ccec3751cc3bea1b11d.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425954} {:answer/id #uuid "722f7e6a-002b-544e-97b2-40986c6598f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/1d/1de0fbb5b6a44423038b980a1e57e1486f02335e1a317ee143f6a6dfa76e7911.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425961} {:answer/id #uuid "d49d4e89-b150-588d-b862-2ff8d4d1e8e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/a7/a7fe5877fd1ec762f6d9ebdeceb8b6739d204081430db291ad3e1284a63d12eb.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425967} {:answer/id #uuid "d882ad0a-e078-5ea7-908f-611bb3476cea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/c1/c139a1b3b413a1cbf60789de2cdc831055b1407c101e4fa63992a814f44cc78d.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425968}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1a94059a-c75b-54d5-86b6-d7a3d7e98d53" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/8c/8c80576fe81dd0978e5e8a4ecd937c5e71e60297dcc94ccec3751cc3bea1b11d.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425954} :answer-field/id #uuid "fd267c3d-501f-5503-9b5e-c946c034c0d4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425976}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "713f4e9c-4d96-5c9b-be62-26529dd25eb1" :question/math-academy-id "q-175390" :question/problem "Consider the following predicate:\n\n$\\,$ $P(x,y):$ $x+y\\le 0,$\n\nwhere the universal set is ${R}^{2}.$ Which of the following shaded regions represents the truth set of the predicate?" :question/worked-solution "The *truth set* of a predicate $P({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n})$ is the set of $n$-tuples in its universal set $U={U}_{1}\\times {U}_{2}\\times ⋯\\times {U}_{n}$ such that substituting these tuples for the variables makes the predicate a true statement:\n\n$$\nT=\\{({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n})\\in U\\,|\\,P({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n})\\}\n$$\n\nThe universal set for our predicate is $U={R}^{2}.$\n\nWe need to find $(x,y)\\in U$ such that the following is true:\n\n$\\,$ $x+y\\le 0$\n\nNow, we convert the inequality into the slope-intercept form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+y & \\le 0 \\\\ y & \\le -x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, let's sketch the truth set $T$ of $P(x,y):$\n\n![](images/1e/1e8f03a8b229a8b2e46af33c700dec57a8abed693a58c75b6312e2ae5a6856c1.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186481668 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198281 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9f9703bd-92ae-51f7-902b-251a7947ba6a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Truth Set of a Multivariable Predicate"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "34edf70b-723f-5261-ad29-e021c72a2740" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/c8/c8d307b09344ecba6c9412edd9e89dc6a7b723117e85ac8e2995af31ac52bc36.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481596} {:answer/id #uuid "3b6e0f3c-e66d-5670-9f6b-a1d8e8d3ec26" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/b8/b85a63b7a77b057d2fd81e4890f9c2ee35b5ae6f1bb3cedfe3203ed68f2d4080.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481598} {:answer/id #uuid "5704fa4b-54ad-5908-b5f1-f9b8c86cf289" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/1b/1b73fdc417e59f631f821989a2a12f34cc7abc1d7c220cad667c07d3f5556c1c.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481603} {:answer/id #uuid "b9713476-1578-522a-9962-a958111f1a0c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/96/9658f04618246f6c35ab0d22c7998accb5708791cdfc756cd276654b7e8fb18a.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481627} {:answer/id #uuid "ed9d83e8-3eed-527f-b289-9b339765d1b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/57/57281b013e998ca0450f7ef5ff7e203495e89b577040b2a2fb17c161896e62ea.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481644}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b9713476-1578-522a-9962-a958111f1a0c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/96/9658f04618246f6c35ab0d22c7998accb5708791cdfc756cd276654b7e8fb18a.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481627} :answer-field/id #uuid "0cc62668-b9db-5986-a4dc-ae1caed64a15" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481651}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9aa267d9-9214-57a8-8b47-8d7c0275750b" :question/math-academy-id "q-175392" :question/problem "Consider the following predicate:\n\n$\\,$ $P(x,y):$ $4{x}^{2}+9{y}^{2}-36>0,$\n\nwhere the universal set is ${R}^{2}.$ Which of the following shaded regions represents the truth set of the predicate?" :question/worked-solution "The *truth set* of a predicate $P({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n})$ is the set of $n$-tuples in its universal set $U={U}_{1}\\times {U}_{2}\\times ⋯\\times {U}_{n}$ such that substituting these tuples for the variables makes the predicate a true statement:\n\n$$\nT=\\{({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n})\\in U\\,|\\,P({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n})\\}\n$$\n\nThe universal set for our predicate is $U={R}^{2}.$\n\nWe need to find $(x,y)\\in U$ such that the following is true:\n\n$\\,$ $4{x}^{2}+9{y}^{2}-36>0$\n\nLet's first rearrange our inequality as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{x}^{2}+9{y}^{2}-36 & >0 \\\\ 4{x}^{2}+9{y}^{2} & >36 \\\\ \\frac{4{x}^{2}}{36}+\\frac{9{y}^{2}}{36} & >1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4} & >1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom here, we see that this represents an ellipse centered at $O$ with semi-axes $3$ and $2.$\n\nFinally, let's sketch the truth set $T$ of $P(x,y):$\n\n![](images/96/9658f04618246f6c35ab0d22c7998accb5708791cdfc756cd276654b7e8fb18a.png)"}]}
